an. for hepatiis A, E screening','2026-05-19 14:17:32','07:05:32 AM','2026-05-31 15:56:36','2026-05-31 15:56:36'),(21,NULL,'pending','local',NULL,NULL,156,2,'Fever \r\nabdominal pain\r\nnausea\r\nLMP = ?3/12\r\n\r\nO/e GCS\r\nASS ?cyesis\r\nplan \r\nto do pt\r\nregister for ANC if positive\r\nheamatinics\r\nomperazole 20mg bd for 2 weeeks','2026-05-19 14:17:32','07:05:32 AM','2026-05-31 16:01:21','2026-05-31 16:01:21'),(22,NULL,'pending','local',NULL,NULL,157,2,'4month old baby \r\nbrough by the aunt with complian of catarrh for 1 week\r\ncough productive of sputm\r\n\r\no/e conscious and active not in distress anicteric acyansed not dehydarated nill peadal edema\r\nplan\r\nsyr azithromycin 70mg daily for 5 days\r\nsyrup vit c 2.5ml dail for 2/52\r\nto do fbc mp','2026-05-19 14:17:32','07:05:32 AM','2026-05-31 16:07:38','2026-05-31 16:07:38'),(23,NULL,'pending','local',NULL,NULL,158,2,'c/o abdominal pain \r\n\r\nclaims to be pain form op site for CS done 3 years ago LMP=3/52\r\nno vommiting but complains of nausea\r\ncomplain of low grade fever intermtent\r\nno discharge, feeling of incomplete voiding\r\n\r\no/e conscious and orinted not in any pain\r\n\r\nAss ? malaria\r\n\r\nplan \r\nto do mp fbc, abdominoplevic scan\r\ntab pcm 1 g tds \r\ntab act 80/480 at 0, 8 then BD for 48hr','2026-05-19 14:17:32','07:05:32 AM','2026-05-31 16:16:03','2026-05-31 16:16:03'),(24,NULL,'pending','local',NULL,NULL,159,2,'A 17-year-old female, apparently well until 24 hours before presentation, was brought in by her relative with inability to pass urine for 24 hours, severe perianal pain, and a four-month history of recurrent constipation characterized by passage of hard stools. The symptoms began after she passed a hard, formed stool while using the toilet 24 hours ago. Soon afterward, she developed significant perianal pain and was unable to void urine. There is no provided history of fever, abdominal trauma, or previous similar episodes. no rectal bleeding, no weight loss, no foreign body insertion. diet mostly cabonhydrate.\r\n\r\no/e in painful distress anicteric acyanosed not dehydrated nill pedal edmao\r\n\r\nabdomen- suprapubic fulness and tendernes\r\n\r\nAss ?internal heamorrohoid with BOO\r\n\r\nPLAN\r\nadmit\r\npass urethral catherter\r\niv pcm 600mg stat\r\nivf 0.9% normal saline 1L 8 houlry alternate with 5%dw 1L 8hourly\r\nliquid parafin 10ml BD- sit up  for 30mins after taking X3days\r\ncouncel on liberal fluid intake,  fiber diet, sitting for long, strainging','2026-05-19 14:17:32','07:05:32 AM','2026-05-31 19:46:30','2026-05-31 19:46:30'),(25,NULL,'pending','local',NULL,NULL,159,2,'Tab pcm 1g TDS','2026-05-19 14:17:32','07:05:32 AM','2026-05-31 19:48:27','2026-05-31 19:48:27'),(26,NULL,'pending','local',NULL,NULL,160,2,'A 10-month-old infant was brought by the parents with a two-week history of diarrhea and vomiting. The diarrhea is described as watery, non-bloody, and non-mucoid. There is no history of passage of blood or mucus in the stool.\r\nThe vomiting has been occurring mostly after feeds and is described as non-bilious and non-projectile. There is no history of hematemesis.\r\nc/o intermittent low-grade fever during this period. There is no provided history of convulsions, abdominal distension, or difficulty breathing.\r\nThe child was apparently well prior to the onset of these symptoms. The history is suggestive of acute watery diarrhea with associated vomiting, and further assessment is required to determine the degree of dehydration and identify any underlying cause.\r\n\r\n\r\no/E lethagic and weak not in distress anicteric acynosed pale1+ nill peadal edema\r\n\r\nv/s PR=124bpm\r\n\r\nAss Acute gastro enteritis with moderate dehydartion\r\n\r\nplan\r\nIVF RL 300ml over 4 hours \r\nIVF 5%DS 350ml over  12houlry\r\nIv cefuroxime 200mg 8 houly\r\niv gentamicin 17mg 12houly after making adequate urine\r\ntab zinc 20mg daily for 10days\r\n70ml of ORS per loose stool\r\nIv artesunate 17mg at 0, 12 24 hours\r\ncontinue breastfeeding and feeding.\r\nto do FBC, EUCR MP','2026-05-19 14:17:32','07:05:32 AM','2026-05-31 20:19:23','2026-05-31 20:19:23'),(27,NULL,'pending','local',NULL,NULL,160,2,'A 10-month-old infant was brought by the parents with a two-week history of diarrhea and vomiting. The diarrhea is described as watery, non-bloody, and non-mucoid. There is no history of passage of blood or mucus in the stool. The vomiting has been occurring mostly after feeds and is described as non-bilious and non-projectile. There is no history of hematemesis. c/o intermittent low-grade fever during this period. no history of convulsions, abdominal distension, or difficulty breathing. The child was apparently well prior to the onset of these symptoms. \r\n\r\no/E lethagic and weak not in distress anicteric acynosed pale1+ nill peadal edema v/s PR=124bpm\r\n\r\n Ass Acute gastro enteritis with moderate dehydartion\r\n\r\n plan IVF RL 300ml over 4 hours IVF 5%DS 350ml over 12houlry Iv cefuroxime 200mg 8 houly iv gentamicin 17mg 12houly after making adequate urine tab zinc 20mg daily for 10days 70ml of ORS per loose stool Iv artesunate 17mg at 0, 12 24 hours continue breastfeeding and feeding. to do FBC, EUCR MP','2026-05-19 14:17:32','07:05:32 AM','2026-05-31 20:21:46','2026-05-31 20:21:46'),(28,NULL,'pending','local',NULL,NULL,172,37,'OPD Review\r\nA 20yr old Nullipara whose is currently on her period presented with  complains of ;\r\n            LAP\r\n            Fever\r\n            Body pains\r\n            Headache\r\n O/e Gc stable\r\n       BP= 110/70mmHg\r\nASS; ? Malaria\r\nPlan\r\n- Do MP\r\n- See with result','2026-05-19 14:17:32','07:05:32 AM','2026-06-01 18:06:18','2026-06-01 18:06:18'),(29,NULL,'pending','local',NULL,NULL,173,37,'OPD\r\nA 5yr old male child brought by the father on account of the following \r\n                          -Cough\r\n                         - Fever\r\n                         -Poor appetite\r\n                         -Paleness\r\n                   